        "symmetry": {
          "value": "balanced-asymmetrical",
          "unit": "none",
          "kind": "measured",
          "source": "ranch-style.proportional_system.symmetry"
        }
      },
      "rule": "Asymmetrical facade organized by the competing claims of the entry and the garage: no vertical hierarchy survives at all, and where a ranch elevation looks well proportioned it is because someone controlled the ridge line, the head datum, and the position of the garage by eye.",
      "note": "Fixes a cascade bug: the resolved kit previously inherited 'strict-bilateral-odd-bay' (eclectic-revivals + colonial-revival, via the family splice), which directly contradicts this node's own stated symmetry attribute and its own defining_characteristics item 8."
    },
    "roof_form": {
